    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "Both parties should read this. The disputed SGD 6.00 cancellation fee is refunded in full to the rider.\n\nThe facts are largely agreed and the platform's own records settle them. The driver did reach the pickup: the trip record shows an 'arrived' event at 18:20:20 and a driver-side termination at 18:25:30 under RIDER_NO_SHOW, and the GPS trace places all 34 of his fixes 24.01 m from the Tampines MRT Exit D private-hire bay — well inside the 150 m arrival radius for a TRANSPORT_HUB. Measured as POL-NS-01(c) requires, from the first in-geofence fix at 18:20:00 and not from the arrival tap, he held position for 330 seconds, 30 seconds over the 300-second minimum, with no gap and a max_gap_sec of 0.0. So the driver's account that he waited inside the geofence is corroborated, and there is no false-arrival marker under POL-NS-05.\n\nThat does not decide the case. POL-NS-04 exonerates the rider where three things hold together, and all three do. (a) The rider sent two locating messages inside the waiting window: 'I am at Exit D under the green sign. Where is your car?' at 18:21:00 and 'I still cannot see you. Please reply.' at 18:23:25. (b) The driver never answered: the 120-second window opened by the 18:21:00 message closed at 18:23:00 with no reply, trip_record.in_app_calls is empty, and no in-app voice call was made at any point before the 18:25:30 cancellation. (c) The rider's device was at the pickup: all 16 of its fixes qualify, spanning 18:20:30 to 18:25:30, at a mean reported distance of 41.9 m, inside the 200 m presence radius for a TRANSPORT_HUB. The rider was where they were supposed to be and was actively trying to coordinate; the silence was the driver's.\n\nPOL-NS-04 is one of the clauses POL-NS-01 itself names as displacing its baseline charge. Because it applies, the cancellation fee is not chargeable and is refunded in full, and the clause states no driver compensation is payable. The driver's POL-NS-07 claim to 80 percent (SGD 4.80) therefore fails — not because the arrival and dwell findings are wrong, which they are not, but because POL-NS-07 pays only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full and no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces it. The driver's own submission correctly identified POL-NS-04 as the exposure. The POL-NS-03 wrong-entrance route does not apply either: 24.01 m is inside the arrival radius, not the 400 m band outside it, so no pin-ambiguity goodwill arises.\n\nI have checked the escalation triggers and none fires. rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 0; both disputes_with_counterparty_90d counters are 0, so POL-NS-09(c) is not met; and the POL-NS-07 anti-farming test does not trip — 1 no-show termination against 120 completed trips, below both the '4 or more' count and the 0.08 rate. The lifetime prior_no_show_flags counters (2 on the driver, 1 on the rider) are context only under POL-GEN-01 and carry nothing here. No two admissible artifacts contradict each other on arrival, dwell or rider presence.\n\nThe SGD 6.00 refunded is the cancellation_fee line on the fare breakdown (payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00), which reconciles with the fee schedule: the GREATER of the TRANSPORT_HUB zone-class fee (SGD 6.00) and the RYDE_PLUS vehicle-tier fee (SGD 6.00). No artifact is impaired on any limb of POL-NS-08 — 20 seconds of clock skew against the 90-second limit, no sampling gap and 34 fixes against the 6-fix floor, 3 chat messages matching trip_record.chat_message_count of 3 with an unbroken msg_id sequence, and a cancellation line equal to the schedule figure — so the finding rests on full-weight evidence. The missing traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-09106-01, weight 0.0) is relied on by neither side and has no bearing; the driver needed no accumulated-dwell extension, as his 330 seconds is a single continuous run."
  },
